I feel compelled to note that no one has ever been diagnosed with
pneumonoetc, nor has any doctor seriously considered it.  It is a
facticious word, created and used exclusively as an example of a very
long word.  It plausibly *could* mean "a disease of the lungs caused
by inhalation of very fine silicate dust as is present in volcanoes,"
and it's a bit funny, so some dictionaries list it.  This does not, in
my opinion, make it a word.

Discussions of the longest word in English always break down into
debates about what counts as a word and what does not, so I won't
continue the exercise.

